# Omnivorous Flytrap's trigger has an intervening "if there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard" (CR 603.4,
# 702.138a). Bot1's graveyard is empty: the Flytrap enters without a trigger (the bare refusal: no target is asked for) and, on
# turn 3 it attacks with one type in the graveyard (Lightning Bolt, an instant, cast at Bot2) and again triggers nothing: it deals its 2
# combat damage plus the Bolt's 3 (20 -> 15) and has no counters. The graveyard of four types is the other scenario.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Omnivorous Flytrap
Lightning Bolt
Plains
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
